  {
    "episode_id": 83453,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83453.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "Here's the problem, I don't think that impeachment of him, even though his dereliction of duty is beyond measure, but the problem is, is the person above him and the administration above him, Joe Biden and the administration doesn't want to deal with the problem, so he just becomes the yes man of saying there's not a real big problem. So there in lies where the people want to impeach him because of his lack of doing his job. Will that gain us ground? No. What will gain us ground is that an administration, whether this one or another one, wakes up to the fact that we have to shut and close down every part of our border except those entrances where we can check and make sure that those coming across are coming across for the right reasons, have the right papers, and can be monitored in a way that we control our borders like every other nation. Look, the thing is, impeachment, I was involved in the impeachment in the state of Illinois, I've arrived to go ahead with it, which the state constitution in Illinois is a lot weaker charge for impeachment. So if you want to talk about the legal side, impeachment, he has to have high crimes in misdemeanors. A terrible job is not necessarily a high crime in Mr. Meener, but it is a reflection of the administration.",
