  {
    "episode_id": 83453,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83453.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "What cheating basically is is that China overloads a product and reduces the product so that U.S. companies can't stay in business because China floods the market. We call it dumping. Now, Trump tried to deal with that and did a great job of dealing with it. And if you remember, several years ago, Trump actually passed what was known as 232, and basically because it endangered this national security by what China was doing with the terrorists and everything like that, that were put on China, made it to where we put people back to work in Granite City. That being said, that is just one industry. So what this legislation does, it doubles the penalties on the violation of trade laws by China, which occurs all the time. They've been cheating for a long time. If you're in any industry that provides everything from steel to electronic device, everything, they flood the market and that is what the problem is, is that we should have never let them in the world trade organizations. But basically what we're doing with this legislation is we're sharpening the teeth. on the existing laws so that we then can implement and make sure that we are not being beat by China by their violation of international trade laws.",
