    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83453.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "I do. Let me let me explain that too. So I was chairman when we're in the majority, I was chairman of the steel caucus. And whenever we're worse, the Democrats are take over that. So there's bipartisan groups that understand what's going on with our trade laws. It's really wild because it's both companies and union people as well that understand what is happening, why China needs to be clamped down on with what they continue to do in the world markets. So yeah, it is a bipartisan thing that can happen.",
