    "turn_text": "We're going to be working together, conservatives as well. I mean, the speaker is having the input of those of us who understand and he's led the charge on this. And let me explain this. The best way I can describe it is if you give your child a credit card and they go to school at the university and they're off by themselves the first time and they all of a sudden run the credit card up. You as the responsible person and you have to still pay the debt, but you have to figure out what you've got to do to put in place. So that child that abused the credit card isn't able to abuse it again. So the national debt, don't confuse the national debt. with the debt ceiling. And the reason I'm saying that is because we're not granting more spending, we're paying for what Joe Biden already blew. And that's a problem. So now what we're doing is, and this is where we're saying this, we will give a limited debt ceiling because we can't go, we've got a payer bill. Our economy and the world cannot take it that we would not actually have our debt ceiling where it needs to be. But we don't raise it too high. We don't do it for a long period of time. And with it, we tie certain things to make sure that we reduce for all. One thing that we're doing is clawing back a lot of the COVID money that these agencies got, but they aren't spending. We've got several lists that we're putting together as conservatives to bring about the changes that fit this ministration and then binding them by law. See, all the president wants is he just wants us to increase the debt ceiling so he can keep doing stupid stuff. We're not going to do that. He's like the child that has went off to college that has ruined the credit card and now we've got to take and get it under control. And that's exactly what we're working together to do. There's many of us that we agree and disagree on certain items. We're going to work together. to get this problem straightened out with the long-term goal of stopping the bad behavior of the administration.",
